[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3795814857","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115344#issuecomment-3795814857","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115344","id":3795814857,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iP4nJ","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-25T01:44:42Z","updated_at":"2026-01-25T01:44:42Z","body":"I suspect you have `res://addons/my_custom_dock/my_dock.tscn` scene opened in the editor. There would be an additional print every time this scene is opened in the editor if it contains presented `@tool` script (it runs in the editor in its own scene too).\n\nI can't reproduce the issue, I got only one print from the plugin itself. +Potential additional prints when opening the mentioned scene in the editor, but that's not a bug.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3795814857/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3796485567","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115344#issuecomment-3796485567","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115344","id":3796485567,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iScW_","user":{"login":"charjr","id":102669158,"node_id":"U_kgDOBh6bZg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102669158?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr","html_url":"https://github.com/charjr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-25T11:37:33Z","updated_at":"2026-01-25T11:40:55Z","body":"> I suspect you have `res://addons/my_custom_dock/my_dock.tscn` scene opened in the editor. There would be an additional print every time this scene is opened in the editor if it contains presented `@tool` script (it runs in the editor in its own scene too).\n\nI did ✔️ \n\nClosing the scene reduced the number of prints by one. Relaunching the editor, I now only see **2** prints.\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1005\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8c504c44-68c2-4db6-8ec4-ad3aaebe1438\" />\n\nAs you can see, I have _nothing_ open at all, yet the dock still calls `enter_tree` twice. \n\n> I can't reproduce the issue, I got only one print from the plugin itself. +Potential additional prints when opening the mentioned scene in the editor, but that's not a bug.\n\nEDIT: I have found the cause for the last print. With the layout I had moved the dock from it's _default_ place. So when Godot launches, it loaded the tree, in it's default place. Then updated to my custom layout. which caused the tree to enter elsewhere.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3796485567/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3796491766","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115344#issuecomment-3796491766","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115344","id":3796491766,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iSd32","user":{"login":"charjr","id":102669158,"node_id":"U_kgDOBh6bZg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102669158?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr","html_url":"https://github.com/charjr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charjr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-25T11:42:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-25T11:42:49Z","body":"@kleonc Thank you for the help.\n\nOne case was as you said, it was an open scene.\nThe other case was unexpected which is that the scene calls `enter_tree` in its original dock, before calling `exit_tree` and then `enter_tree` to the user's custom layout.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3796491766/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3796542870","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115344#issuecomment-3796542870","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115344","id":3796542870,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iSqWW","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-25T12:21:33Z","updated_at":"2026-01-25T12:21:33Z","body":"> The other case was unexpected which is that the scene calls `enter_tree` in its original dock, before calling `exit_tree` and then `enter_tree` to the user's custom layout.\n\nWhile this might be a little unexpected, note the same would happen (exiting/entering the editor scene tree) e.g. on dragging the EditorDock to different slot. So multiple calls shouldn't really be an issue. If you'd want a one time callback then e.g. `_ready` or `_init` could be used instead of `_enter_tree`.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3796542870/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]